  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 37a0d561b0b9aa944bea4668652065db, type: 3}
  m_Name: StationObject
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::TutorialObject
  tutorial:
  - clip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: a795eebfc58a74a4ba54f78dba433af0, type: 3}
    TutorialText: Scattered throughout the system, these stations keep your delivery
      ship running by offering repairs, cooling systems, and refueling. You can easily
      spot a station's specific service by its color. Approaching a station triggers
      the detector system, alerting you to its position with a directional arrow.
  - clip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 257240ecd57d05e468c1e7f89743844d, type: 3}
    TutorialText: "Docking isn't required\u2014simply close the distance to initiate
      automated station maintenance. Watch the station\u2019s outer barrier; when
      its glowing outline extinguishes, your ship's fuel, hull integrity, and performance
      boosts have been fully restored. Don't linger too close after servicing. Initiating
      a full dock will lock your ship down and fail the current delivery."
